      "status": "confirmed",
      "reasoning": "All three earlier selections agree with the supplied graphs and their own captured solutions. For q-78132, the graph is continuous at -2 and 3, but has unequal one-sided limits at 1, so I and III only are true. For q-48062, the hole at (1,1) leaves f(1) undefined while both one-sided limits equal 1; only II is true. For q-48065, f(2)=1 and both one-sided limits equal 1, so all three statements are true. The corner at x=2 does not prevent continuity.",
