      "reasoning": "Fourteen selections have answers established by their own captured worked solutions. Two image selections, q-48082 and q-48038, cannot be resolved: only image paths are supplied, and the solution-image paths differ from every current choice path. No image equivalence can be established from filenames. For q-121221, translation maps (2,3) to (4,4). For q-186866, (x,y) maps to (x-1,-2y), so the original maximum (-1,4) becomes the minimum (-2,-8). For q-78132, the source describes continuity at -2 and 3 and a jump at 1. For q-48088, it identifies discontinuities at -3 and 0. For q-48062, equal one-sided limits exist, but the function value is undefined, making only II true. For q-48065, the limit and function value both equal 1, making all three statements true. For q-13613, rational-root candidates have reduced numerators dividing 10 and denominators dividing 3; only the listed value 3 violates this necessary condition. Candidate status does not guarantee an actual root. For q-39033, factoring gives (3x+5)(x^2-5), with three distinct real roots whose sum is -5/3. Its worked solution incorrectly calls rational-root candidates 'roots'; specifically, -1 is not a root because f(-1)=-8. This wording error does not change the final answer. For q-112076 and q-80107, the leading terms imply respectively left-down/right-up and left-up/right-down behavior; the captured solutions identify A and D. For q-38624, the reported odd degree, negative leading coefficient, and negative intercept uniquely select the listed cubic. For q-38626, the reported even degree, negative leading coefficient, and positive intercept uniquely select the listed quartic. For q-38580, the reported end behavior implies odd degree and positive leading coefficient. For q-38617, both ends tending downward imply even degree and negative leading coefficient, making only III true. Graph conclusions rely on the captured textual descriptions; the images themselves are not rendered in the supplied material. No earlier submitted answers or grades were supplied.",
